# Session Discipline

Always-on conduct. (The deployed-skill-cache guardrail is **Claude-surface only** —
it catches edits to a cloud-synced bundle *outside* this workspace, which Cursor
rules cannot see — so it is not mirrored here.)

## Session log (wrap-up)

At the end of any substantive turn, append a reverse-chron entry to
`docs/SESSIONS.md` — append-only, **link out** (never restate canonical values).
Five fields: Focus / Shipped (branch+commit) / Decisions-defects (link the
ADR/brief) / Open-next / Live-ops state. Carry the prior entry's **Open / next**
forward so the next session resumes without re-deriving state. Skip trivial /
read-only turns. Grounding: `feedback_session_log_discipline` (owner
`docs/operational_rules.md §7`).

## Fetch before a multi-step build

Before scaffolding, building out, or implementing a pipeline/stage/runner/harness,
run `git fetch origin && git log --oneline origin/main ^HEAD | head -20` and grep
for your target files. This repo runs from concurrent worktrees; a parallel
branch may already have landed the work (PR #325's PR-2 was mooted this way).
Reconcile before executing; re-fetch before pushing. Grounding:
`feedback_check_origin_main_before_multistep_build` +
`feedback_recent_gitlog_before_scaffolding_call`.

## Falsifier before a brief

Before authoring anything in `docs/briefs/` or `docs/adr/`, run the <5-min cheap
falsifier PARENT-side and write against the empirical number, not the theoretical
magnitude (one-shot script, 1-CSV sanity sweep, sha256 byte-identity, oracle-tier
pre-check). Use the brief-authoring skill for structure; verify every Rule-0 read
is real (handoff-verify). Grounding: `lesson_run_cheap_falsifier_before_authoring`
+ `feedback_run_falsifier_before_brief`.
